"macOS draws a frame for every refresh: 30 Hz leaves the most of the emulated CPU to apps, at the cost of choppier animation; 60 Hz is smoother. Faster disk writes order them without waiting for a full sync; a sudden power loss could lose the last ones. Quicker wake keeps an idle CPU watching for work for 50 µs, at some battery cost. Superblocks let translated code run past conditional branches. Changes apply the next time a Mac starts." = "刷新率越高，模拟 CPU 用于绘制画面的负担越大。30 Hz 可以为应用留出更多算力，但动画不如 60 Hz 流畅。加快磁盘写入可能增加意外断电时的数据丢失风险；快速唤醒会增加耗电；超级块属于实验功能。相关设置在下次启动 Mac 时生效。";
